    "title": "Adding and subtracting integers",
    "summary": "Add and subtract integers.",
    "skill_codes": [
      "S2"
    ],
    "content_schema_version": 1,
    "content": {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Adding and subtracting integers"
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "Zero pairs"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "When you add integers with different signs, a positive chip and a negative chip cancel. Each pair equals zero."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Example: -5 + 3. Start with 5 negative chips. Add 3 positive chips. Three pairs cancel. Two negatives remain. -5 + 3 = -2."
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "image_asset": "lesson/lesson-2/chip-model-zero-pairs.png",
          "image_alt": "Five negative chips and three positive chips with three zero pairs canceling"
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "Adding same signs"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Same signs: add the distances and keep the sign."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet_list",
          "items": [
            "(-4) + (-3) = -7",
            "4 + 3 = 7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "subheading",
          "text": "Subtracting"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Subtracting an integer is the same as adding its opposite. a - b = a + (-b). Example: 4 - (-3) = 4 + 3 = 7."
        },
        {
          "type": "video",
          "video_code": "VID-INTEGER-ADD-SUBTRACT",
          "segment_start_seconds": 80,
          "segment_end_seconds": 125
        },
        {
          "type": "worked_example",
          "title": "Adding and subtracting",
          "problem": "Compute -7 + 4 and 5 - (-2).",
          "steps": [
            "Step 1: -7 + 4 has different signs. 7 - 4 = 3, and the larger distance is negative.",
            "Step 2: 5 - (-2) means 5 + 2."
          ],
          "answer": "Answer 1: -3. Answer 2: 7."
        },
        {
          "type": "common_mistake",
          "text": "4 - (-3) = 1 is wrong. Subtracting -3 means adding 3, so 4 - (-3) = 7."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "cta",
          "text": "Ready to practice. Continue to the regular exercise for 6 questions."
        }
      ],
      "source_text": "Lesson 2.1 - Adding and subtracting integers\nSkill: S2\nObjective:\n1. Add and subtract integers.\nZero pairs\nWhen you add integers with different signs, a positive chip and a negative chip cancel. Each pair equals zero.\nExample: -5 + 3. Start with 5 negative chips. Add 3 positive chips. Three pairs cancel. Two negatives remain. -5 + 3 = -2.\nAdding same signs\nSame signs: add the distances and keep the sign.\n(-4) + (-3) = -7\n4 + 3 = 7\nSubtracting\nSubtracting an integer is the same as adding its opposite. a - b = a + (-b).\nExample: 4 - (-3) = 4 + 3 = 7.\nWorked example\nProblem: Compute -7 + 4 and 5 - (-2).\nStep 1: -7 + 4 has different signs. 7 - 4 = 3, and the larger distance is negative. Answer 1: -3.\nStep 2: 5 - (-2) means 5 + 2. Answer 2: 7.\nCommon mistake\n4 - (-3) = 1 is wrong. Subtracting -3 means adding 3, so 4 - (-3) = 7."
    }
  },
